number one.

282
00:10:54,797 --> 00:10:57,613
A truck with a fourteen percent chance

283
00:10:57,613 --> 00:10:59,169
is above the average,

284
00:10:59,169 --> 00:11:00,725
and it may cost less,

285
00:11:00,725 --> 00:11:02,355
and be easier to find.

286
00:11:02,535 --> 00:11:04,539
The ranking is a guide for the

287
00:11:04,539 --> 00:11:07,144
whole market, not only for the winners.

288
00:11:07,495 --> 00:11:10,308
Let's think about what a probability like

289
00:11:10,308 --> 00:11:13,601
thirty-one point nine percent means in practice.

290
00:11:13,781 --> 00:11:15,751
It does not mean that a Ram

291
00:11:15,751 --> 00:11:18,451
three thousand five hundred has a one

292
00:11:18,451 --> 00:11:20,420
in three chance of lasting,

293
00:11:20,420 --> 00:11:23,558
and a Silverado three thousand five hundred

294
00:11:23,558 --> 00:11:25,600
HD has a one in nine chance.

295
00:11:25,780 --> 00:11:26,793
It means that,

296
00:11:26,793 --> 00:11:29,396
across all the trucks of that model,

297
00:11:29,396 --> 00:11:32,143
about that share are expected to reach

298
00:11:32,143 --> 00:11:33,083
that mileage.

299
00:11:33,263 --> 00:11:34,593
For any single truck,

300
00:11:34,593 --> 00:11:36,619
the care it gets matters as much

301
00:11:36,619 --> 00:11:37,443
as the model.

302
00:11:37,793 --> 00:11:39,857
That is why the same model can

303
00:11:39,857 --> 00:11:41,646
show up on both sides of a

304
00:11:41,646 --> 00:11:42,541
conversation.

305
00:11:42,721 --> 00:11:45,200
One owner has a truck that passed

306
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:48,355
three hundred thousand miles with only oil

307
00:11:48,355 --> 00:11:48,956
changes.

308
00:11:49,136 --> 00:11:52,007
Another had a transmission fail at one

309
00:11:52,007 --> 00:11:53,292
hundred thousand.

310
00:11:53,472 --> 00:11:54,409
Both are real,

311
00:11:54,409 --> 00:11:56,282
and both are in the average.

312
00:11:56,462 --> 00:11:59,328
A buyer who checks the service history

313
00:11:59,328 --> 00:12:01,816
of a specific used truck has more

314
00:12:01,816 --> 00:12:04,532
information than any study can give,

315
00:12:04,532 --> 00:12:06,342
and should use it first.

316
00:12:06,692 --> 00:12:08,946
There is also the question of what

317
00:12:08,946 --> 00:12:10,140
counts as lasting.

318
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:13,149
A truck can reach two hundred fifty

319
00:12:13,149 --> 00:12:15,817
thousand miles with a new engine,

320
00:12:15,817 --> 00:12:18,403
a new transmission and a new set

321
00:12:18,403 --> 00:12:21,152
of suspension parts along the way.

322
00:12:21,332 --> 00:12:24,006
The study estimates the odometer reading,

323
00:12:24,006 --> 00:12:25,898
not how much was spent to get

324
00:12:25,898 --> 00:12:26,289
there.

325
00:12:26,469 --> 00:12:28,402
So a truck on this list can

326
00:12:28,402 --> 00:12:30,335
still be expensive to keep,

327
00:12:30,335 --> 00:12:32,197
and a truck that is not on

328
00:12:32,197 --> 00:12:33,342
it can be cheap.

329
00:12:33,522 --> 00:12:36,808
Longevity and cost are different questions.

330
00:12:37,158 --> 00:12:38,140
For a buyer,

331
00:12:38,140 --> 00:12:40,923
the practical lesson is to use the

332
00:12:40,923 --> 00:12:42,560
ranking as a filter,

333
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:43,706
not a verdict.

334
00:12:43,886 --> 00:12:45,818
If you want a truck to keep

335
00:12:45,818 --> 00:12:47,321
for a very long time,

336
00:12:47,321 --> 00:12:49,826
start with the group that sits near

337
00:12:49,826 --> 00:12:52,044
the top, the heavy-duty trucks,

338
00:12:52,044 --> 00:12:53,905
the Tundra and the Tacoma.

339
00:12:54,085 --> 00:12:56,677
Then check the exact model year,

340
00:12:56,677 --> 00:13:00,159
the engine, the recalls and the maintenance

341
00:13:00,159 --> 00:13:00,807
records.

342
00:13:00,987 --> 00:13:03,627
The study narrows the list from dozens

343
00:13:03,627 --> 00:13:05,225
of trucks to a handful.

344
00:13:05,405 --> 00:13:07,622
The rest is your own inspection.

345
00:13:07,973 --> 00:13:09,807
And what about new trucks?

346
00:13:09,987 --> 00:13:12,102
The study can only look at trucks

347
00:13:12,102 --> 00:13:14,026
that have been on the road for

348
00:13:14,026 --> 00:13:14,410
years.

349
00:13:14,590 --> 00:13:17,778
A truck built in twenty twenty-six has

350
00:13:17,778 --> 00:13:19,792
no odometer history yet.

351
00:13:19,972 --> 00:13:21,457
So when you buy new,

352
00:13:21,457 --> 00:13:24,279
you are relying on the company's track

353
00:13:24,279 --> 00:13:25,838
record, the warranty,

354
00:13:25,838 --> 00:13:27,472
and the early reports.

355
00:13:27,652 --> 00:13:29,770
That is one more reason to read

356
00:13:29,770 --> 00:13:31,069
the warranty terms,

357
00:13:31,069 --> 00:13:33,255
and to check what happens if the

358
00:13:33,255 --> 00:13:34,759
model is discontinued,

359
00:13:34,759 --> 00:13:37,014
as the Nissan Titan was after the

360
00:13:37,014 --> 00:13:39,064
twenty twenty-four model year.

361
00:13:39,415 --> 00:13:41,493
Now the twist we promised.

362
00:13:41,673 --> 00:13:43,434
Look at who is not on the

363
00:13:43,434 --> 00:13:43,786
list.

364
00:13:43,966 --> 00:13:45,688
The Ford F-one-fifty,

365
00:13:45,688 --> 00:13:49,788
the Chevrolet Silverado one thousand five hundred,

366
00:13:49,788 --> 00:13:52,822
the Ram one thousand five hundred and

367
00:13:52,822 --> 00:13:56,184
the GMC Sierra one thousand five hundred,

368
00:13:56,184 --> 00:13:59,545
the four best-selling pickups in America,

369
00:13:59,545 --> 00:14:02,087
are not among the top twelve in

370
00:14:02,087 --> 00:14:03,563
twenty twenty-six.

371
00:14:03,743 --> 00:14:05,183
In the earlier edition,

372
00:14:05,183 --> 00:14:08,001
they were between eleventh and fourteenth for

373
00:14:08,001 --> 00:14:10,004
the F-one-fifty, Sierra and Ram,

374
00:14:10,004 --> 00:14:11,882
with the Silverado at seventh.

375
00:14:12,232 --> 00:14:15,039
That means the trucks that most Americans

376
00:14:15,039 --> 00:14:17,024
buy are not the ones that the

377
00:14:17,024 --> 00:14:19,557
study thinks are most likely to last.

378
00:14:19,737 --> 00:14:22,816
The heavy-duty trucks and the two Toyotas

379
00:14:22,816 --> 00:14:23,116
are.

380
00:14:23,296 --> 00:14:25,588
That does not mean the half-ton trucks

381
00:14:25,588 --> 00:14:26,071
are bad.

382
00:14:26,251 --> 00:14:28,961
Those four brands sold more than one

383
00:14:28,961 --> 00:14:31,898
and a half million pickups through nine

384
00:14:31,898 --> 00:14:34,006
months, heavy-duty included.

385
00:14:34,186 --> 00:14:36,516
It means that the work trucks,

386
00:14:36,516 --> 00:14:38,380
built for heavier loads,

387
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:40,167
tend to survive longer,

388
00:14:40,167 --> 00:14:41,953
according to the model.

389
00:14:42,133 --> 00:14:44,584
A bigger frame and a bigger engine

390
00:14:44,584 --> 00:14:45,953
are built for more.

391
00:14:46,303 --> 00:14:48,009
Think about what that means.

392
00:14:48,189 --> 00:14:49,048
If you tow,

393
00:14:49,048 --> 00:14:51,389
and haul, and plan to keep the

394
00:14:51,389 --> 00:14:52,638
truck for years,

395
00:14:52,638 --> 00:14:55,213
the heavy-duty trucks make sense.

396
00:14:55,393 --> 00:14:57,802
If you drive mostly on the highway,

397
00:14:57,802 --> 00:15:00,142
and the truck is a family vehicle,

398
00:15:00,142 --> 00:15:02,551
a half-ton truck is built for that,

399
00:15:02,551 --> 00:15:04,478
and the study says it is not

400
00:15:04,478 --> 00:15:07,231
the likeliest to reach two hundred fifty

401
00:15:07,231 --> 00:15:07,851
thousand.

402
00:15:08,031 --> 00:15:10,103
But how many families keep a truck

403
00:15:10,103 --> 00:15:10,713
that long?

404
00:15:10,893 --> 00:15:13,829
If you drive fifteen thousand miles a

405
00:15:13,829 --> 00:15:17,322
year, two hundred fifty thousand miles takes

406
00:15:17,322 --> 00:15:19,147
almost seventeen years.

407
00:15:19,498 --> 00:15:22,993
Let's compare two figures we already saw,

408
00:15:22,993 --> 00:15:25,465
because the comparison helps.

409
00:15:25,645 --> 00:15:28,592
The Ram three thousand five hundred is

410
00:15:28,592 --> 00:15:31,150
at thirty-one point nine percent,

411
00:15:31,150 --> 00:15:34,329
and the Tacoma is at twenty-five percent.

412
00:15:34,509 --> 00:15:36,467
That is a gap of six point

413
00:15:36,467 --> 00:15:39,102
nine points, but both are far above

414
00:15:39,102 --> 00:15:41,963
the truck average of eleven point one.

415
00:15:42,143 --> 00:15:43,053
For a buyer,

416
00:15:43,053 --> 00:15:45,707
the lesson is that second place and

417
00:15:45,707 --> 00:15:48,134
fourth place are both very good.

418
00:15:48,314 --> 00:15:50,407
Do not pay a large premium to

419
00:15:50,407 --> 00:15:52,284
move up one spot in a list

420
00:15:52,284 --> 00:15:53,294
like this one.

421
00:15:53,645 --> 00:15:56,129
So who do these results suit?

422
00:15:56,309 --> 00:15:59,112
A rancher, a contractor or a farmer

423
00:15:59,112 --> 00:16:01,834
who tows and hauls heavy loads and

424
00:16:01,834 --> 00:16:04,477
keeps a truck for a decade should

425
00:16:04,477 --> 00:16:07,039
start with the heavy-duty group,

426
00:16:07,039 --> 00:16:09,922
the Ram three thousand five hundred,

427
00:16:09,922 --> 00:16:13,285
the Sierra three thousand five hundred HD,

428
00:16:13,285 --> 00:16:15,767
and the Ford Super Duty trucks.

429
00:16:15,947 --> 00:16:18,305
A buyer who wants a smaller truck

430
00:16:18,305 --> 00:16:19,306
that holds up,

431
00:16:19,306 --> 00:16:21,950
and does not need that much capacity,

432
00:16:21,950 --> 00:16:23,807
should look at the Tacoma.

433
00:16:23,987 --> 00:16:26,282
A buyer who wants a half-ton with

434
00:16:26,282 --> 00:16:28,647
a strong record can start with the

435
00:16:28,647 --> 00:16:31,011
Tundra, after checking the engine.

436
00:16:31,362 --> 00:16:32,744
And who should wait,

437
00:16:32,744 --> 00:16:34,334
or look somewhere else?

438
00:16:34,514 --> 00:16:36,945
If you are choosing a midsize truck,

439
00:16:36,945 --> 00:16:39,443
remember that the Ford Ranger and the

440
00:16:39,443 --> 00:16:41,806
Nissan Frontier were not in the top

441
00:16:41,806 --> 00:16:42,954
twelve this time.

442
00:16:43,134 --> 00:16:45,294
That does not make them bad trucks.

443
00:16:45,474 --> 00:16:47,771
It means the study does not single

444
00:16:47,771 --> 00:16:49,797
them out, so you need to check

445
00:16:49,797 --> 00:16:52,567
the individual truck even more carefully.

446
00:16:52,747 --> 00:16:55,853
A buyer who wants the strongest longevity

447
00:16:55,853 --> 00:16:58,504
signal in the midsize group has one

448
00:16:58,504 --> 00:17:00,700
clear answer in this ranking,

449
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:02,291
and it is the Tacoma.

450
00:17:02,641 --> 00:17:04,672
Here is the first common mistake.

451
00:17:04,852 --> 00:17:06,971
People read a list like this and

452
00:17:06,971 --> 00:17:09,023
then buy any used truck of that

453
00:17:09,023 --> 00:17:11,737
model, without checking that exact truck.

454
00:17:11,917 --> 00:17:13,836
A model can be near the top,

455
00:17:13,836 --> 00:17:15,960
and one truck of that model can

456
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:17,536
still have been abused.

457
00:17:17,716 --> 00:17:20,236
The second mistake is the reverse.

458
00:17:20,416 --> 00:17:23,349
A buyer ignores a perfectly good truck

459
00:17:23,349 --> 00:17:25,743
because its model is not in the

460
00:17:25,743 --> 00:17:26,592
top twelve.

461
00:17:26,772 --> 00:17:30,142
Remember that the study measures averages across

462
00:17:30,142 --> 00:17:31,125
a whole model,

463
00:17:31,125 --> 00:17:33,301
not the history of the truck in

464
00:17:33,301 --> 00:17:34,214
front of you.

465
00:17:34,564 --> 00:17:36,859
So how do you verify a specific

466
00:17:36,859 --> 00:17:37,304
truck?

467
00:17:37,484 --> 00:17:41,082
Start with the vehicle identification number,

468
00:17:41,082 --> 00:17:41,721
the VIN.

469
00:17:41,901 --> 00:17:43,998
Use it to look up open recalls

470
00:17:43,998 --> 00:17:46,865
in the official government recall search,

471
00:17:46,865 --> 00:17:49,521
and ask the seller for the maintenance

472
00:17:49,521 --> 00:17:51,619
records that go with that VIN.

473
00:17:51,799 --> 00:17:55,235
Ask whether the engine or transmission was

474
00:17:55,235 --> 00:17:57,116
ever replaced, and why.

475
00:17:57,296 --> 00:17:59,189
Then ask for the answers in writing.

476
00:17:59,369 --> 00:18:01,482
A seller with a good truck is

477
00:18:01,482 --> 00:18:03,741
usually happy to share records,

478
00:18:03,741 --> 00:18:06,365
and a seller who avoids the question

479
00:18:06,365 --> 00:18:08,041
has told you something.

480
00:18:08,392 --> 00:18:09,958
If you are buying new,

481
00:18:09,958 --> 00:18:12,734
the same logic applies to the warranty.

482
00:18:12,914 --> 00:18:15,564
Ask for the warranty terms in writing,

483
00:18:15,564 --> 00:18:18,424
and compare the out-the-door price of two

484
00:18:18,424 --> 00:18:20,029
trucks on the same day,

485
00:18:20,029 --> 00:18:21,354
with the same trim.

486
00:18:21,534 --> 00:18:23,498
A truck that is likely to last

487
00:18:23,498 --> 00:18:25,332
is only a good deal when you

488
00:18:25,332 --> 00:18:27,165
do not overpay at the start.

489
00:18:27,345 --> 00:18:29,970
The Tacoma at thirty-nine thousand,

490
00:18:29,970 --> 00:18:32,820
four hundred fifty dollars for the SR5

491
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:34,171
is a good example,

492
00:18:34,171 --> 00:18:36,496
because the price on the lot is

493
00:18:36,496 --> 00:18:38,746
not the price in the headline.

494
00:18:39,096 --> 00:18:41,114
One last thought on the trucks that

495
00:18:41,114 --> 00:18:42,497
drop out of the ranking.

496
00:18:42,677 --> 00:18:44,200
The Ford F-one-fifty,

497
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:47,100
the Silverado one thousand five hundred,

498
00:18:47,100 --> 00:18:49,783
the Ram one thousand five hundred and

499
00:18:49,783 --> 00:18:52,683
the Sierra one thousand five hundred are

500
00:18:52,683 --> 00:18:55,004
all missing from the top twelve,

501
00:18:55,004 --> 00:18:58,049
yet millions of people drive them happily.

502
00:18:58,229 --> 00:18:59,301
If you own one,

503
00:18:59,301 --> 00:19:01,445
this is not a reason to worry.

504
00:19:01,625 --> 00:19:03,398
It is a reason to keep up

505
00:19:03,398 --> 00:19:06,235
the maintenance, and to keep the service

506
00:19:06,235 --> 00:19:06,803
records.

507
00:19:06,983 --> 00:19:09,261
Records are the one thing every owner

508
00:19:09,261 --> 00:19:11,540
controls, and they also help when you

509
00:19:11,540 --> 00:19:11,847
sell.

510
00:19:12,027 --> 00:19:14,156
A buyer will pay more for a

511
00:19:14,156 --> 00:19:16,915
truck with a clear history than for

512
00:19:16,915 --> 00:19:18,018
one with none.

513
00:19:18,369 --> 00:19:20,265
So what should you check before you

514
00:19:20,265 --> 00:19:22,432
buy a used truck in twenty twenty-seven?

515
00:19:22,612 --> 00:19:24,493
First, the service records,

516
00:19:24,493 --> 00:19:27,140
because a truck that was maintained is

517
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:29,439
more likely to last than one that

518
00:19:29,439 --> 00:19:29,996
was not.

519
00:19:30,176 --> 00:19:33,465
Second, the recalls and the known problems

520
00:19:33,465 --> 00:19:35,110
for the exact engine.

521
00:19:35,290 --> 00:19:37,558
Third, the mileage and the age,

522
00:19:37,558 --> 00:19:38,216
together.

523
00:19:38,396 --> 00:19:39,954
And fourth, the price,

524
00:19:39,954 --> 00:19:42,361
because a truck that lasts is only

525
00:19:42,361 --> 00:19:44,131
a good deal if you do not

526
00:19:44,131 --> 00:19:45,617
overpay at the start.

527
00:19:45,968 --> 00:19:47,673
We put all of this into a

528
00:19:47,673 --> 00:19:51,424
checklist, the Twenty Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide.

529
00:19:51,604 --> 00:19:53,682
It covers the numbers to check,

530
00:19:53,682 --> 00:19:55,692
the questions to ask a dealer,

531
00:19:55,692 --> 00:19:58,373
and the warning signs we walked through.

532
00:19:58,553 --> 00:20:00,752
The link is in the description and

533
00:20:00,752 --> 00:20:02,175
in the pinned comment.

534
00:20:02,355 --> 00:20:04,848
If you want to know which engines

535
00:20:04,848 --> 00:20:06,736
to avoid in a used truck,

536
00:20:06,736 --> 00:20:09,681
subscribe, because that is coming soon.

537
00:20:09,861 --> 00:20:10,987
Thanks for watching.
